\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Frozen symbolic transport across the homotopy. Panel (a) reports return-gap parity polarity and panel (b) reports finite exposure. Development, validation, sealed-test, and neighboring-\(a\) curves are overlaid in the two panels. All four neighbors reproduce near-unit parity at \(\rho =0.10\) and \(0.20\), while the parent-derived carriers collapse near the symplectic endpoint. The endpoint \(P\) is conditional on rare pre-escape fragments and cannot pass the exposure gate.}}{6}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:transport}{{1}{6}{Frozen symbolic transport across the homotopy. Panel (a) reports return-gap parity polarity and panel (b) reports finite exposure. Development, validation, sealed-test, and neighboring-\(a\) curves are overlaid in the two panels. All four neighbors reproduce near-unit parity at \(\rho =0.10\) and \(0.20\), while the parent-derived carriers collapse near the symplectic endpoint. The endpoint \(P\) is conditional on rare pre-escape fragments and cannot pass the exposure gate}{figure.1}{}}
